{
  "quest.373B87566F6879E4.title": "&aPrecision Parts",
  "quest.3A9912660456ECB4.title": "&aSplinters and Conduits",
  "quest.5A0473F1679DECB4.title": "&3Souls at Work",
  "quest.677D909854D44D88.quest_desc": [
    "Saronite tools match Netherite for damage and speed, with 2,031 durability, and need no smithing upgrade. Repair them with Saronite Ingots.",
    "",
    "The &3Saronite Sword&r and &bSaronite Arrows&r harvest souls in the field. Deal the killing blow while carrying an empty glass bottle and the soul goes straight into it. Without a bottle, a spirit appears that you can catch later.",
    "",
    "Undead still have no soul to give.",
  ],
  "quest.2396B89E788E2AC4.title": "&aYellow Crystals",
  "quest.50EC812A64C866C4.quest_desc": [
    "&aFoci&r is the casting item. Left-click to pick a spell and right-click to cast. Spells are paid from fresh soul bottles in your inventory or a carried Soul Gem, and the empty bottles come back.",
    "",
    "You start knowing &bGrowth&r and &bMend&r, each costing one Benign soul. Try Growth next to some crops.",
    "",
    "&cSouls stored in a Soul Well can't pay for spells.&r Bottle some back out before you head off. A failed cast costs nothing.",
  ],
  "quest.663CDBB5BF71F88D.title": "&3Soul Forge",
  "quest.16EB9AC35AA09D8F.title": "&dSaronite Armor",
  "quest.3C1956BE24C1C90A.title": "&aCircuit Stamper",
  "quest.1843C0EE7E7D05F3.title": "&3The Rest of the Workshop",
  "quest.39304DE6B081D6D4.title": "&dGod Soul",
  "quest.78397E6469FC9213.quest_desc": [
    "&eAnima&r is soul magic built from bones and crystal. You bottle the souls of living creatures and spend them on spells, rituals and machines. Further along you forge a new metal, build a golem you can pilot and make a god of your own.",
    "",
    "The &aNecronomicon&r is the mod's guide. Its tabs run in the same order as this chapter, and JEI has a page for every workstation too.",
    "",
    "Most of the work happens out in the world. Cages, glassware, wells and rituals are all built by hand, and each quest here says what the in-world step is.",
    "",
    "[\"\", \"Infusions, offerings, research and soul work also level your \", {\"text\": \"Magic skill tree\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ftb:skills,ftb:magic.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Skill Trees guide\"}}, \".\"]",
  ],
  "quest.6D4A7E25E55FA2F4.quest_desc": [
    "A &aGem Mold&r turns one bucket of &3Molten Blue Crystal&r into three &2Blue Gems&r.",
    "",
    "You'll need a lot of them. Every &bControl Circuit&r takes one, the Soul Stone for a Soul Well takes twelve, and relays, shrines and offering plates use them too. Planting extra crystal clusters now saves waiting later.",
  ],
  "quest.438379200FFAFBBD.quest_desc": [
    "Each piece of &3Soulbone armor&r is its own infusion, and the four use different souls: Unhinged for the helmet, Doomed for the chestplate, Predatory for the leggings and Benign for the boots.",
    "",
    "It matches diamond for protection and durability, adds 5% knockback resistance per piece and repairs with Crystallized Soulbone. It's also the base for Saronite armor, and enchantments carry over when you upgrade.",
  ],
  "quest.466547590C6E3ED5.quest_desc": [
    "Place three &5Offering Plates&r directly beside a &dDeity Shrine&r, on any three of its four sides. Put one of each of a god's code items on the plates and right-click the shrine with an empty hand. The items are used once to dedicate it.",
    "",
    "From then on, right-click the shrine holding the god's &bsacred item&r to worship. You can worship once every five minutes, and five times in a row to the same god makes you &bdevout&r.",
    "",
    "&cWorshipping any other god resets the count.&r Two shrines to the same god let you Sneak + Right-click to travel between them for one worship.",
  ],
  "quest.337B905F5A2641FC.title": "&aBone Cage",
  "quest.45F0B6AEF1FEE061.title": "&aSoul Well",
  "quest.78397E6469FC9213.title": "&eAnima",
  "quest.1873AA084EDB5E67.title": "&3Golem Part Assembler",
  "quest.1EF4C37FCAEC99E8.quest_desc": [
    "The &3Corporeal Reconstructor&r brings undead back to life. Place it in the middle of a 5x5 area with eight Soul Stone around it at the same height, and a &aBone Cage&r directly on top. The guide's preview shows where the stones go.",
    "",
    "Close an undead creature in the cage with a Wise soul in a well within 32 blocks. After 10 seconds it becomes a living villager. A zombified piglin becomes a piglin instead, and it stays one in the Overworld.",
    "",
    "Restored villagers have souls again, which makes this a steady source of &3Wise&r souls.",
  ],
  "quest.5A0473F1679DECB4.quest_desc": [
    "Anima's machines run on &bworkers&r, souls they pull one at a time from the nearest Soul Well within 32 blocks. A worker lasts 20 durability, or 30 in a machine that favors its kind, and each job wears it down.",
    "",
    "The &3Idol of Harvesting&r is a good first machine. It harvests and replants mature crops in a 7x7 area around it, and it favors &aBenign&r souls.",
    "",
    "&cA redstone signal pauses a machine&r, and breaking one destroys its worker. If nothing happens, check the nearest well and its Keep filters first.",
  ],
  "quest.1843C0EE7E7D05F3.quest_desc": [
    "Six more machines draw from the same well.",
    "",
    "- &3Soul Placer&r: places blocks from its inventory. Favors Ender.",
    "- &3Soul Breaker&r: breaks the block in front of it with the tool you give it. Favors Doomed.",
    "- &3Idol of Gathering&r: pulls in loose items nearby. Favors Aquatic.",
    "- &3Idol of Shepherding&r: shears sheep in a 9x9 area. Favors Predatory.",
    "- &3Idol of Breeding&r: breeds animals in a 9x9 area until there are 12. Favors Benign.",
    "- &3Idol of Forestry&r: fells trees and replants them. Favors Unhinged.",
    "",
    "The Placer and Breaker face away from the side you click, like a log.",
  ],
  "quest.1E3E7B27B205D155.quest_desc": [
    "Pour water onto ordinary stone, then drop one &aSoulbone&r and one &fLapis Lazuli&f into it close together. A young &2Blue Crystal&r cluster replaces the water.",
    "",
    "A cluster grows through three stages of 10 minutes each, and only while its chunk is loaded. Right-click it with an empty hand to check the stage. Break a mature cluster with a pickaxe for two crystals, then plant one back on stone and keep the other.",
    "",
    "Crystals grow on stone, deepslate and most cut or polished stone. &cCobblestone and dirt don't work.&r Start several clusters at once, since you'll go through a lot of crystals.",
  ],
  "quest.373B87566F6879E4.quest_desc": [
    "These four parts go into every big machine from here on.",
    "",
    "- &aEmitter&r: two go into each Quantifier, and the Soul Forge and Pantheon take one directly.",
    "- &2Ponderance Lattice&r: needs a Yellow Gem. The Infusion Table and Golem Fabricator each take one.",
    "- &3Quantifier&r: the most expensive part at five circuits, and the Infusion Table needs one.",
    "- &bSoul Relay&r: the Infusion Table needs one and the Soul Forge needs three.",
    "",
    "Placed in the world, relays also guide loose spirits to a well. Keep them at most 10 blocks apart.",
  ],
  "quest.307221FA2971AFE5.quest_desc": [
    "Place the &3Golem Fabricator&r with three blocks of clear height and right-click the rack to fit each part. Then use a &3Soul Leash&r on the finished golem to take control.",
    "",
    "The golem has 50 hearts and 27 cargo slots. It mines, fights and picks up drops, and the &bToggle Golem Mining Mode&r key switches it to 3x3 digging. Repair it with Iron Ingots from outside.",
    "",
    "&cYour own body stays where you left it and can be attacked&r, so leave it somewhere safe.",
  ],
  "quest.786B4144CD27D566.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Ring of Power&r gives you survival flight while you carry it. Double-tap jump to start flying.",
    "",
    "It takes five &dGod Souls&r, four on the plinths and one offered at the table, so plan on several boss kills. Each ocean monument has three Elder Guardians.",
    "",
    "A dropped ring never despawns, and only lava destroys it. Taking it off mid-flight gives 10 seconds of slow falling.",
  ],
  "quest.307221FA2971AFE5.title": "&3Workshop Golem",
  "quest.677D909854D44D88.title": "&3Saronite Sword",
  "quest.75D6CEA6F7167770.title": "&aSoul Gem",
  "quest.61E2C9FEA985422F.title": "&3Ceremonial Robe",
  "quest.16FCA08F989F3C8C.title": "&fSoulbone",
  "quest.3A9912660456ECB4.quest_desc": [
    "Stamping a &aSoulbone&r gives six &2Soulbone Splinters&r, and up to four bones fit in one press.",
    "",
    "Splinters and redstone then stamp into &aSoulbone Conduits&r, three at a time. One Soulbone ends up as enough conduits for two Control Circuits.",
  ],
  "quest.1E3E7B27B205D155.title": "&aBlue Crystals",
  "quest.65DFAC0AEF26F533.title": "&aControl Circuit",
  "quest.75D6CEA6F7167770.quest_desc": [
    "A &aSoul Gem&r is a pouch for soul bottles, with four slots that each hold a stack of 16. Right-click it to open it.",
    "",
    "Spells and Altar of Souls offerings draw from any Soul Gem you carry. &cThe Infusion Table is the exception&r and wants the soul bottle in your hand.",
  ],
  "quest.3D6BB0B2FDF36444.title": "&3New Knowledge",
  "quest.77B1E32B1A1835F0.quest_desc": [
    "Build the line at the height of the cage's lower block. The &aFunnel&r goes directly behind the cage, opposite the doors, and the four glassware pieces follow it in a row, each touching the one before.",
    "",
    "{image:ftb:textures/quests/anima/soul_extraction_setup.png width:180 height:104 align:center}",
    "",
    "Close the cage on a grown living creature and power the Funnel. One piece is checked each second, and green means correct. &cThe first wrong piece turns red and stops the attempt&r, but nothing is lost.",
    "",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Replace only the first red piece, switch the Funnel's power off and on, and try again. When all four pass, a spirit appears at the exit. Right-click it with a glass bottle.",
    "",
    "Each soul kind keeps the same sequence for the whole world, so write it down once you find it.",
    "",
    "Use an empty bottle on the soul to get a &2Benign Soul&r.",
  ],
  "quest.77B1E32B1A1835F0.title": "&aYour First Soul",
  "quest.548BFB6396968E63.quest_desc": [
    "Making your own god is optional. Place the &dDeity Fabricator&r on Soul Stone with three blocks of height, and a plinth three blocks out to the north, east, south and west.",
    "",
    "Put a God Soul on one plinth and three different items on the others. Those three items become the god's code, and the combination must be unused. Pick things you can gather again, since every shrine needs a set.",
    "",
    "Right-click the fabricator to name the god and choose its blessing, curse, power, sound and look. Its sacred item is used up with each worship, so make it something common.",
  ],
  "quest.7B11D59F8E2D62E9.quest_desc": [
    "&3Raw Saronite&r needs a &2Doomed&r soul for its infusion. Doomed souls come from witches, illagers and cave spiders, so a pillager outpost or a witch hut is a good place to stock up.",
    "",
    "&cA regular furnace can't smelt it.&r Only the Soul Forge can.",
  ],
  "quest.61E2C9FEA985422F.quest_desc": [
    "You have to wear the &3Ceremonial Robe&r to use the Altar of Souls. Foci spellcasting works without it.",
    "",
    "It protects like a leather tunic and takes chest enchantments. Repair it at an anvil with Shadoweave Cloth. The &3Spirit Thread&r that goes into it also makes the &bSoul Leash&r you'll want for golems.",
  ],
  "quest.1EF4C37FCAEC99E8.title": "&3Corporeal Reconstructor",
  "quest.65DFAC0AEF26F533.quest_desc": [
    "The &aControl Circuit&r is the part you'll make most. Nearly every Anima machine uses at least one, and the bigger ones use several.",
    "",
    "Each circuit also takes a Blue Gem, so keep the Blow Mold busy while you stamp.",
    "",
    "&7&oA Quantifier uses five circuits once you count the two inside each of its Emitters.&r",
  ],
  "quest.39304DE6B081D6D4.quest_desc": [
    "A &dGod Soul&r comes from the Ender Dragon, the Wither, the Warden or an Elder Guardian. The killing blow has to be a direct strike from the &3Saronite Sword&r, with an empty glass bottle in your inventory.",
    "",
    "&cArrows don't work, and without a bottle the soul is lost.&r A defeated god avatar gives one as well.",
    "",
    "God Souls can't go into a Soul Well or power machines. One makes a god, and five make a Ring of Power.",
  ],
  "quest.663CDBB5BF71F88D.quest_desc": [
    "The &3Soul Forge&r uses worker souls instead of fuel. Place it within 32 blocks of a stocked Soul Well.",
    "",
    "Raw Saronite becomes a &3Saronite Ingot&r in 10 seconds for 5 worker durability. The forge also smelts ordinary furnace recipes at normal speed for the same cost per item.",
    "",
    "A worker lasts 20 durability, or 30 if it's an &6Infernal&r soul, the kind the forge favors. Hoppers feed it from the top or sides and empty it from below.",
  ],
  "quest.786B4144CD27D566.title": "&6Ring of Power",
  "quest.5CD3D480A4BE3226.quest_desc": [
    "The &6Deity Hammer&r calls down an existing god's avatar for a boss fight. It needs open sky, a clear 5x5 area eight blocks tall, and three Offering Plates beside it holding the god's code items.",
    "",
    "The avatar has 900 health and three phases. Leave the marked circles, jump the expanding ring and sidestep the line of light. Each extra player adds 75% to its endurance.",
    "",
    "&cWinning deletes that god for good&r, along with its shrines and Priest Rods. Finish it with the Saronite Sword and a bottle for a God Soul. The ritual won't start on Peaceful.",
  ],
  "quest.7B11D59F8E2D62E9.title": "&3Raw Saronite",
  "quest.47A9BFB7EF1C8724.title": "&3Crystallized Soulbone",
  "quest.456D538288C1E710.title": "&aYellow Gems",
  "quest.21E67245D140A48B.quest_desc": [
    "Gods in Anima are made by players and shared by the whole server. The &dPantheon&r lists every one, most worshipped first, with its three &bcode items&r, its effects and its sacred item.",
    "",
    "&cYou don't need your own god to worship.&r Pick one from the Pantheon, note its code items and build it a shrine.",
  ],
  "quest.375892AEFA92CDE7.quest_desc": [
    "While devout, right-click one of your god's shrines with a &dPriest Rod&r to bind it to that god.",
    "",
    "Left-click the rod to choose an action, then right-click to cast. Each cast costs one worship.",
    "",
    "- &aBlessing&r: the god's blessing on devout players within 16 blocks for 60 seconds.",
    "- &cCurse&r: the god's curse on everyone else within 16 blocks, monsters included, for 15 seconds.",
    "- &6Power&r: the god's special power, usable only while it leads the Pantheon or ties for the lead.",
  ],
  "quest.2228AFBC2F153AAE.title": "&3Altar of Souls",
  "quest.548BFB6396968E63.title": "&dDeity Fabricator",
  "quest.28C03305E26EABB8.quest_desc": [
    "Souls are pulled out through a line of blown &bGlassware&r. Make the Funnel Mold and the four glassware molds, then blow one &aFunnel&r and a few of each piece.",
    "",
    "The four pieces are &bDecanters, Splitters, Gourds and Spirals&r. Any of them can fill any of the line's four positions, and a sequence can use the same piece more than once.",
    "",
    "Each piece is one batch from one molten bucket. Blow at least four of every kind before you start, so you can swap pieces freely while you work out the sequence.",
  ],
  "quest.47A9BFB7EF1C8724.quest_desc": [
    "&3Crystallized Soulbone&r comes from your first infusion, and most of what follows needs it, from armor to Raw Saronite to the Altar of Souls.",
    "",
    "JEI's &bSoul Infusion&r page lists the plinth items in clockwise order starting from north. If no rune appears, check the nine supports and that order before anything else.",
    "",
    "Take the floating result with an empty hand, or put a hopper under the table.",
  ],
  "quest.45F0B6AEF1FEE061.quest_desc": [
    "Twelve &aSoul Stone&r make a Soul Well. Lay them flat in a 5x5 square, three along each side, leaving the four corners and the middle 3x3 empty. The portal forms by itself. Leave two blocks of headroom above the frame.",
    "",
    "Right-click the well with bottled souls to deposit them and get the bottles back. It holds 64 of each kind.",
    "",
    "Soul-powered machines take their &bworkers&r from the nearest loaded well within 32 blocks. &cA nearer empty well blocks a farther full one&r, and breaking the frame releases every stored soul.",
    "",
    "&7&oSet a kind to Keep in the well's filter screen to stop machines from using it.&r",
  ],
  "quest.37BF2F11443D3895.title": "&3Research Table",
  "quest.2228AFBC2F153AAE.quest_desc": [
    "The &3Altar of Souls&r trades four souls of one kind plus a matching item for a random enchanted book. Wear the robe, hold a soul bottle and right-click either half of the altar.",
    "",
    "- &aBenign&r with a Golden Carrot: Protection, Feather Falling or Fortune.",
    "- &3Wise&r with an Emerald: Mending, Efficiency or Unbreaking.",
    "- &dEnder&r with an Eye of Ender: Silk Touch, Infinity or Projectile Protection.",
    "",
    "The guide lists the other five kinds. &cOne offering in ten gives a curse instead.",
  ],
  "quest.1873AA084EDB5E67.quest_desc": [
    "Golems are built part by part on the &3Golem Part Assembler&r. Put one ingredient on each side holder in any order, then power it with redstone for two seconds.",
    "",
    "Right-click the output to collect it and free the holders. &aCondensed Stone Plates&r and &3Armored Plates&r go into every body part, so make plenty of both.",
    "",
    "&7&oTools in a recipe must be undamaged, and they're used up.&r",
  ],
  "quest.375892AEFA92CDE7.title": "&dPriest Rod",
  "quest.77016F4C944C984C.title": "&aGlassworking",
  "quest.16FCA08F989F3C8C.quest_desc": [
    "Hold an ordinary &fBone&f in your main hand and deal the killing blow on a grown farm animal. The bone you're holding turns into &aSoulbone&r, one per kill.",
    "",
    "&cUndead have no soul&r, so zombies and skeletons won't work for this. Cows, pigs and sheep are the easy targets.",
    "",
    "Later on there are faster ways. Dropping bones through a wandering spirit converts the whole stack, and kills with a &aSoulbone Spear&r turn normal bone drops into Soulbone, which makes skeletons a steady supply.",
  ],
  "quest.546C442D551C6024.quest_desc": [
    "A golem needs one head, one torso, two arms and two legs. JEI's &bGolem Part Assembler&r page shows every step, from joints and shoulders to the eye and core.",
    "",
    "&cEach arm uses up an undamaged Iron Pickaxe.&r The head takes an anvil and the core takes a Quantifier, so have those ready.",
    "",
    "&7&oAll told, one golem is 18 Armored Plates, which is 36 iron and about 224 stone.&r",
  ],
  "quest.546C442D551C6024.title": "&3Golem Body",
  "quest.7CD1D40C6A6C8C6D.title": "&3Infusion Ring",
  "quest.466547590C6E3ED5.title": "&dShrine and Worship",
  "quest.68F2A958D11A4BDF.title": "&aOther Kinds of Soul",
  "quest.5CD3D480A4BE3226.title": "&6Challenge a God",
  "quest.337B905F5A2641FC.quest_desc": [
    "The &aBone Cage&r holds a creature while you pull out its soul. Place it with two blocks of height and open space at the doors, then right-click to open it.",
    "",
    "An open, empty cage pulls in creatures from six blocks away and shuts when it catches one. The first player to use a cage becomes its keeper, and only the keeper can work the doors by hand. Redstone on either half opens it as well.",
    "",
    "&cOpening or breaking the cage lets the captive go.&r Catch a grown farm animal first, since it gives a &bBenign&r soul.",
    "",
    "{image:ftb:textures/quests/anima/soul_extraction_setup.png width:180 height:104 align:center}",
  ],
  "quest.2396B89E788E2AC4.quest_desc": [
    "Each cluster has about a 20% chance to turn yellow as it matures. A yellow cluster gives a single &aYellow Crystal&r, and it can't be replanted.",
    "",
    "Save every one you find. They go into &bFoci&r, &bQuantifiers&r and Yellow Gems, and the only way to get more is to keep plenty of blue clusters growing.",
  ],
  "quest.28C03305E26EABB8.title": "&aExtraction Glassware",
  "quest.77016F4C944C984C.quest_desc": [
    "&bGlassworking&r needs a &aBlow Mold&r with a &2Bellows&r beside it, nozzle pointing into the basin.",
    "",
    "For material, drop a &aBlue Crystal&r into lava. That lava block turns into molten crystal, and an empty bucket scoops it up. One crystal makes one bucket, which is one batch.",
    "",
    "To blow something, pour the bucket into the basin, right-click the basin with a mold, then right-click the Bellows. ",
    "",
    "After two seconds, right-click the basin to take the output. You keep both the bucket and the mold.",
    "",
    "&7&oGlass blocks and Yellow Crystals make their own molten buckets the same way.&r",
  ],
  "quest.16EB9AC35AA09D8F.quest_desc": [
    "Each Soulbone piece is upgraded on the infusion ring with Saronite Ingots and a Netherite Ingot. Enchantments, name, trim and damage all carry over.",
    "",
    "A full set gives 23 armor, 16 toughness and 60% knockback resistance, and repairs with Saronite Ingots.",
    "",
    "&cThe souls get harder here.&r The helmet wants a Wise soul, the chestplate Infernal, the leggings Predatory and the boots Ender.",
  ],
  "quest.6D4A7E25E55FA2F4.title": "&aBlue Gems",
  "quest.438379200FFAFBBD.title": "&3Soulbone Armor",
  "quest.3C1956BE24C1C90A.quest_desc": [
    "The &aCircuit Stamper&r presses components. It needs no souls, only a lever beside it.",
    "",
    "Stand at the open front with the hinge at the back and right-click a recess floor to place one item. Each recess holds exactly one. Turn the lever on to stamp, then off to open the lid, and right-click to collect.",
    "",
    "Recipes show the grid as seen from the front, so top left and top right are the two recesses nearest the hinge. A wrong pattern leaves the ingredients where they are.",
  ],
  "quest.68F2A958D11A4BDF.quest_desc": [
    "Each creature gives one kind of soul, and each kind has its own extraction sequence to solve.",
    "",
    "- &aPredatory&r: spiders, wolves, foxes, cats and other hunters.",
    "- &2Doomed&r: witches, illagers and cave spiders.",
    "- &aUnhinged&r: creepers, slimes, silverfish, breezes, vexes and ravagers.",
    "- &bAquatic&r: fish, squid and other water creatures.",
    "- &dEnder&r: endermen, endermites and shulkers.",
    "- &6Infernal&r: blazes, striders, piglins and other living Nether creatures.",
    "- &3Wise&r: villagers, wandering traders, allays and iron golems.",
    "",
    "&cBabies, undead and creatures that already gave a soul can't be used.&r JEI's &bSoul Sources&r page shows the kind for every mob, modded ones included.",
  ],
  "quest.456D538288C1E710.quest_desc": [
    "Drop a &aYellow Crystal&r into lava for a bucket of molten yellow crystal, then blow it in the &2Gem Mold&r for three Yellow Gems.",
    "",
    "One batch covers the &bPonderance Lattice&r for your Infusion Table and the eye of your first golem, so a single yellow crystal is enough to start.",
  ],
  "quest.21E67245D140A48B.title": "&dPantheon",
  "quest.3D6BB0B2FDF36444.quest_desc": [
    "Right-click a translated book to learn its spell. The book is used up, and learned spells stay with you through death.",
    "",
    "Stronghold libraries, woodland mansions, ancient cities, bastion treasure rooms and End cities always hold a book. Dungeons, mineshafts, temples and most other vanilla structures have about a one in three chance.",
    "",
    "&cChests added by other mods don't get spell books.&r The rarer spells turn up more often in harder loot.",
  ],
  "quest.7CD1D40C6A6C8C6D.quest_desc": [
    "Infusion is a ritual on a &77x7&r ring. The &3Infusion Table&r sits in the middle with eight &bPlinths&r around it, and all nine stand on &aSoul Stone&r at the same height.",
    "",
    "The north, east, south and west plinths have two empty blocks between them and the table. The diagonal ones sit two blocks out along each axis. The guide's &bVisualize&r button projects the layout for you.",
    "",
    "Load ingredients &cclockwise from north&r. The whole pattern can be rotated as long as the order holds. When a soul rune appears, right-click the table with the listed soul bottle in your hand. The ritual takes 10 seconds and needs no well.",
  ],
  "quest.50EC812A64C866C4.title": "&aFoci and Spells",
  "quest.37BF2F11443D3895.quest_desc": [
    "New spells come from encrypted &aSpell Books&r found in structure chests. The &3Research Table&r translates them, using a worker from a stocked Soul Well within 32 blocks.",
    "",
    "Put the book in the tome slot and &aBlue Crystals&r in the crystal slot. Each attempt takes 15 seconds and one crystal, with a 25% chance to succeed. A failed attempt keeps the book.",
    "",
    "Ordinary books in the tome slot get scribed instead, with a 5% chance of producing an encrypted book. It's slow, but it works if you'd rather not explore.",
  ],
}